.TH SYSTEM 3S
.UC
.SH NAME
system \- issue a shell command 
.SH SYNTAX
.B system(string)
.br
.B char *string;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I System
causes the
.I string
to be given to
.IR sh (1)
as input (as if the string had been typed as a command at a terminal).
The current process waits until the shell has
completed, then returns the exit status of the shell.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
execve(2), wait(2), exec(3), popen(3S), environ(5)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status 127 indicates the shell couldn't be executed.
.SH FILES
/bin/sh
.SH BUGS
.I System
waits for the shell
to complete by using
.IR wait (2).
This may have the undesired side effect of collecting and discarding
the exit status of other processes.
